      },
      "lineNbr": 131,
      "author": {
        "id": 5045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-16T23:02:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Make `CHECK_GT(font_file_stream_object_number, 0u)` instead? Also line 171.",
      "revId": "2def67f76c79150125c1ebfcc2febb5d07209374",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47d90579_9505d50a",
        "filename": "core/fpdfapi/font/cpdf_truetypefont_unittest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 131,
      "author": {
        "id": 5845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-17T02:29:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue is that the gtest assertions return void, so they\u0027re difficult to use inside a function like this (see [documentation](https://google.github.io/googletest/advanced.html#assertion-placement)). `CHECK_OP` things will just crash I think, which isn\u0027t what we want here, as this should log an error and allow the current thread to continue testing. The idea here is to allow `make_font` to be a somewhat \"external\" bit of code and fail by returning nullptr, then the caller can `ASSERT_TRUE` the result.\n\nThat being said, this should never happen, so it\u0027s probably fine to put the `CHECK` here.",
      "parentUuid": "9c3d6d85_2ae74804",
      "revId": "2def67f76c79150125c1ebfcc2febb5d07209374",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
